      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so it's about those subconscious links. to make the training really landing for the executives, could you actually write out a few short 'profiles' or 'candidate summaries'? \n\nfor example, instead of just saying they are perceived as 'less articulate,' could you write a mock internal recruiter note for one candidate with an AAVE dialect and one with a heavy accent, using the kind of language or descriptors an unconscious biased manager might actually write in their notes—like how they'd describe their 'fit' or 'polish' compared to a candidate with a standard accent? i want to show how these biases actually look in writing.",
